---
title: Matcha brownie pudding
servings: 2
prep-time: 15 minutes
cook-time: 40 minutes
tags: [matcha, recipe, baking, dessert, brownie-pudding]
source: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DSN3gfBktIG/
image: https://scontent-iad3-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/598630607_18093168224502575_5462359572329704139_n.jpg?stp=cmp1_dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=102&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=0fHc-KKtgGEQ7kNvwH0j60b&_nc_oc=AdmH6Ptvlpksx873mXP5DxDwZeEWdLwRgvOng9a2Nu5Up0YACT0LwahRlhZAcCyLcCc&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=q4Y9ePYrPA2p9qtjYt66bg&oh=00_AfmWJPSgM7CTF_i85jZzvHKwu9YsAkVfOlkCyCUf-LRmog&oe=694C8B11
---

Preheat your #oven to 350°F. Whisk @egg{2%large} and @granulated sugar{0.5%cup} until light yellow and fluffy. Then whisk in @granulated sugar{4%tbsp}.

Add the flour, matcha, and salt to the egg mixture and whisk just until combined. Add in @coconut oil{4%tbsp} and whisk again.

Lightly oil a #ceramic dish{} and transfer the batter to it. Place the dish into a larger #metal baking pan{} and add enough of the hottest tap water so that the dish is filled halfway.

Bake for ~{40%minutes}. Enjoy